  "constraints": [
    "Only the output of SparseFlashMla, its inverse rotary, zero/copy padding and actual BF16 InplaceCopy Transpose enter the sender. Input rotation, QLI, indexer and diagnostic history transposes excluded. Fixed 8 rank AllToAll count and byte order. Immutable zero send still receives and computes the OA. The no-collective DP at carrier 416 receives no credit.",
    "Each TP8 latest packet advances by the change of max corrected completion across its eight senders. Use saved offset bounds from EP16 count exchanges; no subtraction of exported HCCL elapsed time. Transfer the resulting TP shift through unchanged network, OA/OB and RS to the last DP at EP16. Peer streaming, fixed host submissions or another reader can hide all gains; clock ranges are conditional schedule scenarios, not lower bounds on actual benefit.",
    "free_external makes every old sender task free with unchanged SparseFlashMla time. Separate packer uses the recorded transpose time as replacement for producing the entire packet in one pass and assumes completely hidden rotation. Direct epilogue keeps full recorded rotary time, charges invalid-row share of old pad time and 0%, 25% or 50% of old transpose duration as an added store-layout cost. These are sensitivity scenarios. Keep original full local output if a live reader needs it; the added write, spills, synchronization, reduced MLA utilization and exceptional arithmetic can lower or reverse gains.",
    "Direct output needs the original two FP32 products, original rounding and BF16 final cast in the 64 rotated channels. The other 448 copy unchanged. Current standalone prototype had a changed exceptional BF16 bit in an earlier fixture, failed default graph capture and was slower on all four shapes. No equivalence or performance evidence for a new direct epilogue is implied.",
    "Historical C8 projects clean per-rank 40-layer graph samples to each potentially eligible replay ordinal once across 16 synchronized ranks. Includes unassigned/prompt-adjacent replays before original endpoints and whole own first prompt wave for inclusive TTFT. Min/median/max are empirical references across windows, not a hardware or end-to-end ceiling. Graph, eager, and prior implementation timing cohorts differ. No change to speculative acceptance, host timing, other service work or HCCL traffic.",
    "Ordinary requests use one observed prefill size with same-size valid rows on the active path, interpolated per-layer mean scenario cost from adjacent-size medians, plus counted verification batches times the median clean graph. Padded tail and exact exposed rank at each step are unknown. No credit to inactive padded graph lanes or other requests outside own-step scope; every counted graph uses the original fixed work. The six responses have no production frequency weights."
  ],
